{#- /learn/ (#742): the getting-started course as pages, for somebody who has
    not signed up. The operator's words, 17 Sep 2026: *"or even on the homepage
    as kind of pre-sales documentation. For someone coming to the page cold.
    I could be something like prospektor.ai/learn"*. The words are the mails'
    own (`data/lessons.json`, out of the studio's `public/lessons.js`), drawn
    in the /resources/ idiom: the same hub hero, the same card grid, the same
    ending at the free scan. Four courses, each named after the result at
    its end, the way the Academy draws them (#1191, #1198): the same quiet
    eyebrow the three time-based groups had, kept because a heading that
    names the result says what the steps under it get a cold reader. The
    courses' minutes stay in the product. -#}

<header class="res-hub-hero">
  <div class="res-hub-hero-inner">
    <span class="tag">learn</span>
    <h1 class="res-hub-h1">Nine steps, one press each</h1>
    <p class="res-hub-lede">
      This is the course a new workspace is mailed, one step a day, in four
      short courses. Each course ends in a result: a first meeting from a cold
      company, a warm introduction, one of your competitor's customers, a
      sharper pitch. About {{ lessons.minutes }} minutes in all.
    </p>
  </div>
</header>

<section class="res-hub">
  {%- for group in lessons.groups %}
  <h2 class="learn-group">{{ group.name }}</h2>
  <ul class="res-grid learn-grid">
    {%- for lesson in group.lessons %}
    <li class="res-card">
      <a href="{{ lesson.url }}">
        <span class="res-card-topic">{{ lesson.topic }}</span>
        <h3 class="res-card-title">{{ lesson.subject }}</h3>
        <p class="res-card-dek">{{ lesson.opener }}</p>
        <span class="res-card-meta">Day {{ lesson.day }} of {{ lessons.count }}</span>
      </a>
    </li>
    {%- endfor %}
  </ul>
  {%- endfor %}
</section>

<section class="res-hub-cta">
  <div class="res-hub-cta-inner">
    <span class="tag">try it</span>
    <h2>Read day one on your own company</h2>
    <p>The scan reads your site and says who the studio would go after for you
      and why. It is free, takes about ninety seconds, and is what the first
      lesson opens on.</p>
    <a class="btn-cta" href="/#scan">Scan your site</a>
  </div>
</section>
